<title>UK: UK's CRP Leisure says in acquisition talks.</title>
<headline>UK's CRP Leisure says in acquisition talks.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-12-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>CRP Leisure Plc said it was in detailed discussions for the acquisition of a small group of companies and for a full listing for CRP's shares on the London Stock Exchange.</p>
<p>It said the talks are at an advanced stage but should they fail to be successful by the end of the year, CRP would seek a listing either on the Alternative Investment Market or on OFEX, a market run by brokers JP Jenkins.</p>
<p>The company's shares are currently traded on the Unlisted Securities Market (USM), which is due to close at the end of the year.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
